Question 3

You wrote a Playwright test that passes every time on your machine. In the CI pipeline, it fails about one run in four, with no code changes. The team is starting to ignore the failures and just rerun the pipeline.

How would you investigate this, what are the common causes, and how would you fix it so the team can trust the suite again?

Gather evidence: CI trace, screenshot, video and error; trace on first retry; reproduce with --repeat-each and CI worker count
Find the root cause:
Timing and waits (hard waits, non-retrying assertions)
Test data and dependencies (shared data, order dependence, parallel conflicts)
Environment differences (headless, viewport, timezone, network, unstable environment)
Fragile locators
A real race condition in the app (raise it as a defect)
Fix and verify: fix the cause, use retries only as a safety net, rerun many times in CI
Rebuild trust: quarantine with an owner and deadline, track flaky tests, never dismiss red runs with “just rerun”

